    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Number of national stakeholders who are piloting climate services and early warning mechanisms
2. Number of crisis prevention and recovery plans that use diverse methods to manage multi-dimensional risks
3. Guidelines mainstreaming climate change in recovery processes in cities affected by crisis (0 = no guidelines; 1= guidelines are developed; 2 = guidelines are disseminated)
4. Number of local solar solutions (disaggregated by country)
5. Number of women led initiatives managing local solar solutions
6. Number of people benefiting from increased access to energy, diversified livelihoods or enhanced climate security (disaggregated by gender)
7. Number of country grants that have at least one activity that tackles gender inequality
8. Number of assessments and restoration measures for critical ecosystems implemented (disaggregated by country)
9. Baseline of sustainable finance landscape in the region (0 = no baseline; 1 = baseline surveys underway; 2 = baselines undertaken and validated; 3 = baseline used regularly by other stakeholders)
10. Online knowledge platform launched (0 = none; 1 online platform is ready; 2 = online platform is launched; 3 = online platform is regularly updated)
11. Capacity of select stakeholders, such as commercial financial institutions to develop climate-related financial products and services is strengthened (Low = information and knowledge about financial products is minimal; Medium = exposure to some available financial products; High = relevant stakeholders are able to develop their own products)
12. Number of private sector roundtables organized
13. Coalition of Arab Finance Ministers for Climate Change (0 = Absence of Coalition; 1= Coalition discussions under-way; 2 = established)
14. Number of bankable projects/viable investment propositions ready for financing
15. Number of country case studies 
16. Number of investment theses developed for targeted market segments
17. Number of reports and materials capturing lessons learne</narrative>
    </description>
